GhostHand third-party notices
=============================

This file lists code, designs and ideas borrowed from other projects, with their licenses.
npm dependencies are listed by `bun run license:check`; their notices ship with release builds.

Borrowed ideas (no code copied unless stated)
---------------------------------------------
- Playwright (Apache-2.0, Microsoft): AI aria snapshot format and aria-ref locators, used through the public API.
- browser-use (MIT), Stagehand (MIT), Midscene (MIT), cua (MIT): agent loop and element-table design ideas.
- TypeSafe SDK for JS (@typesafe-ai/sdk, MIT): used as a dependency.
- Playwright Test Agents (Apache-2.0, Microsoft): the Markdown test-plan shape (suites, cases, steps,
  expected results) that QA specs follow.
- cooper667/jev-playwright: preflight step classification (ok/transient/derived/visual/external), advisory
  vs decisive steps, and the one-line verdict for calling agents (ideas only).
- axe-core (MPL-2.0, Deque Systems): used unmodified as a dependency; its script is evaluated in pages under
  test for the QA accessibility score. Source: https://github.com/dequelabs/axe-core
- Model Context Protocol TypeScript SDK (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk, MIT): used as a dependency.
- pi-mono `packages/ai/src/auth/oauth/openai-chatgpt.ts` (MIT, Mario Zechner): structure of the Sign in with ChatGPT loopback/PKCE flow (apps/desktop/src/main/chatgpt), reimplemented from the SIWC docs; no code copied.
- T3 Code `apps/desktop` (MIT): Electron + electron-builder monorepo layout reference.
- cua (MIT, Cua AI): RFC 4268 native-candidate design (role classes, stable ids from role + label + ancestor
  hash, one action per observation), the action-result effect/evidence contract and the element-token
  freshness rules, reimplemented in packages/driver-desktop (ideas only).
- agent-sh/computer-use-linux (MIT, Avi Fenesh): GNOME Wayland pitfalls (keycodes for letters, released
  presses, semantic clicks because AT-SPI extents are untrusted, doctor readiness checks) (ideas only).
- Anthropic claude-quickstarts computer-use-demo (MIT): Xvfb + window manager container recipe (ideas only).
- dogtail and gnome-ponytail-daemon (GPL-2.0, Red Hat and contributors): the headless `mutter --headless`
  + Mutter RemoteDesktop recipe and its pitfalls (warm-up motions, button codes). Ideas only, read from the
  research notes; no code was copied.
- pywinauto (BSD-3-Clause): Invoke watchdog and "semantic vs real input" split (ideas only).
- macapptree (MIT, MacPaw): AX label fallbacks and points-vs-pixels scale (ideas only).

Desktop sandbox image (not distributed by GhostHand; built locally from packages/driver-desktop/hosts/linux/Containerfile)
